package mapdemo

// A map whose VALUE is an UNBOUNDED ARRAY (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.8, §2.9): "A
// VALUE is anything a table field can hold ... and an unbounded `[]T` (§2.9)".
// The value is an ordinary field of the generated entry, so its storage is that
// field's own row, the sixteen-byte list slot (§4.2), and its elements ride in
// the HOLDER'S node extent as any list's do. That is one member, so the handle
// is the slot itself and the list's own surface reaches the elements.

table Spans
{
    tracks map[uint8][]Item // []T: an unbounded extent inside the entry's own
    after  int32
}
